  <ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Viridon Services LLC is an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Viridon Holdings LLC and the service company for the Viridon family of companies (Viridon) providing associate companies with a variety of administrative, management and support services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;On March 28, 2025, Viridon acquired DATC Path 15 Transmission LLC, an owner of an economic interest in an 84-mile, 500-kilivolt transmission corridor in central California.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;This acquisition provided Viridon with operating transmission assets. As a result, Viridon Services has filed its first FERC Form 60 for the year 2025 and therefore prior year results are not included.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Viridon Services LLC does not have borrowed funds and therefore does not bill interest to associate companies.&lt;/span&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
  <ferc:OrganizationChart id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">Viridon Services Org Chart.pdf</ferc:OrganizationChart>
  <ferc:MethodsOfAllocationTextBlock id="f-3" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#211e1e;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Cost Allocation Methods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Identifiable costs will be allocated to the Client Companies and other unaffiliated companies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#211e1e;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; to which the Service Company provides Services so far as costs can be identified and related to the particular transactions involved without excessive effort or expense.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; Costs (not including Non-Allocable Costs) that are for Services of a general nature and cannot be directly assigned, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#211e1e;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;including taxes, interest, other overhead, and compensation for the use of capital, shall be fairly and equitably allocated using the approaches set forth below. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Costs are billed to Client Companies based on one or more of the methodologies listed below: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Direct Billed &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;&#8211; Time, travel expenses and other costs of resources used exclusively for the provision of services that are readily identified with an activity. Direct billed charges can be either external or internal. External direct billed charges are costs paid to third parties on behalf of a Client Company, such as travel expenses, temporary labor, consulting and legal services, insurance and general and administrative costs. Internal direct charges are labor costs, where personnel track time and charge to certain accounts set up to separately capture support for an identified Client Company. Internal labor costs are transferred at a rate that includes the employee&#8217;s actual salary plus adders which cover benefits and administrative costs such as payroll taxes, workers compensation insurance, medical insurance, dental insurance, life insurance, accidental death insurance, long-term disability insurance, 401K and pension contributions, and incentive compensation costs. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-indent:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Direct Cost Ratio (&#8220;DCR&#8221;)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Times New Roman',serif;font-size:12pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt; &#8211; Indirect costs that support the entire Viridon Holdings holding company system rather than individual companies (for example executive management services or human resources), and where a specific cost driver or cost causation may not readily be determined and applied, shall be allocated to each Client Company based on the total direct hours and other costs charged to a Client Company as a percentage of the total Viridon Holdings holding-company-system-wide costs for the same period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:MethodsOfAllocationTextBlock>
